DATA & FILE OVERVIEW\
--------------------\
\
1. File List: \
\
PROCESSED DATA (folder: processed_data):\
\
cleaned_data.csv: FINAL CLEAN DATA SHEET USED IN ANALYSIS. One row per experimental plot per monitoring month (April, May, June 2024), combining plot-level kelp survival and length, plot-level and site-level grazer densities, and site-level environmental and water-quality variables.\
\
cleaned_green_gravel_monitoring_Aug.csv: Cleaned plot-level green gravel monitoring data for the six study sites with August 2024 surveys included (plus derived kelp survival, grazer density and kelp length). August data are not analyzed in the paper (shown in Supplementary Fig. S1).\
\
cleaned_green_gravel_monitoring.csv: Cleaned plot-level green gravel monitoring data with August removed (April to June 2024), with derived kelp survival, grazer density and kelp length. Plot-level input to cleaned_data.csv.\
\
cleaned_monitoring_transects.csv: Site-level urchin and grazer counts from the quadrat transect surveys, summed by site and month and converted to densities (per m2). Site-level input to cleaned_data.csv.\
\
cleaned_ysi_measurements.csv: Bottom temperature, dissolved oxygen, salinity and pH from YSI ProDSS casts, one row per site per monitoring month.\
\
ENV/monitoring_periods.csv: Start and end dates of each monitoring interval at each site, used to summarize logger data between surveys.\
\
ENV/combined_env.csv: Combined EnvLogger (T7.3) bottom temperature time series from all six sites.\
\
ENV/summary_env.csv: Mean and maximum bottom temperature per site and monitoring interval calculated from the EnvLogger data.\
\
ENV/summary_temp.csv: Final mean and maximum bottom temperature per site and monitoring interval (EnvLogger and HOBO temperature records combined); source of the temperature variables in cleaned_data.csv.\
\
ENV/summary_tilt.csv: Mean and maximum current speed per site and monitoring interval from Marotte HS drag-tilt current meters.\
\
ENV/HOBO/combined_hobo.csv: Combined HOBO Pendant logger time series of bottom light and temperature from all six sites.\
\
ENV/HOBO/summary_hobo_light.csv: Mean bottom light (lux) per site and monitoring interval.\
\
ENV/HOBO/summary_hobo.csv: Mean light and mean and maximum temperature per site and monitoring interval calculated from the HOBO data.\
\
RAW DATA (folder: raw_data):\
\
green_gravel_monitoring.csv: Raw plot-level monthly monitoring of outplanted kelp, gravel, and grazers in experimental plots.\
\
urchin_monitoring_transects.csv: Raw quadrat-level grazer counts and habitat notes from the site-level transect surveys.\
\
YSI_measurements.csv: Raw YSI ProDSS water-quality measurements (dissolved oxygen, salinity, temperature, pH) by site and date.\
\
site_coordinates_all.csv (in raw_data/metadata): Latitude and longitude of each study site with its site-level grazer density and nearby kelp forest classification.\
\
ENV/HOBO DATA: have all data from FOLDER/SITE (raw logger files by site).\
\
2. Relationship between files, if important: Environmental (HOBO and ENV logger) data is organized by folder (site name). Each site folder contains a 'combined_dataset.csv' of all loggers from that site over the course of the study.\
\
Processing workflow: raw logger data -> combined_env.csv / combined_hobo.csv -> monitoring-interval summaries (summary_*.csv, using monitoring_periods.csv); raw green_gravel_monitoring.csv -> cleaned_green_gravel_monitoring(_Aug).csv; raw urchin_monitoring_transects.csv -> cleaned_monitoring_transects.csv; raw YSI_measurements.csv -> cleaned_ysi_measurements.csv. \
\
cleaned_data.csv is the merge of cleaned_green_gravel_monitoring.csv, cleaned_monitoring_transects.csv, cleaned_ysi_measurements.csv, summary_temp.csv, summary_hobo_light.csv and summary_tilt.csv, joined by site and month.\
\
